<title>CHINA: China finishes drilling deep oil well in Xinjiang.</title>
<headline>China finishes drilling deep oil well in Xinjiang.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has completed drilling its deepest oil well in the Taklamakan desert in the northwestern region of Xinjiang, the China News Service said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The oil well, with a depth of 5,750 metres, was expected to produce 168 tonnes of crude oil a day and 1.08 million cubic metres of natural gas, the report said.</p>
<p>China invested at least $430,000 in foreign equipment to drill the well, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
